window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["14"]={"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bahrain":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-20T16:20Z","sha":"fa9741946dbd7873c2b71a8df3c7ec43c98ec257390688ccfc97d75ffedcf792","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/bahrain","bytes":80867,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Bahrain travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-18T14:55:22+00:00","mod":"2026-11-18T16:31:19+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional tensions"]},{"k":"p","s":["The context in the Middle East remains deeply unpredictable and the risk of sudden escalation is high. Since conflict began in early 2026, Iran has stated its intention to target locations associated with the US and Israel, including, but not limited to, organisations, businesses, facilities, and institutions. There have been strikes and retaliatory attacks by Iran and others across the region against civilian and military infrastructure. There remains a risk of further attacks across the region at short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals in, or planning to travel through, the Middle East should be prepared for possible flight cancellations, airspace closures, and travel disruptions. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["read ",["If you’re affected by a crisis abroad - GOV.UK","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],". This includes guidance on “how to prepare for a crisis” with suggestions on what you might include in your emergency supplies and “what to do in a crisis”"]},{"k":"li","s":["sign up to ",["FCDO Travel Advice email alerts","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bahrain/email-signup"]]},{"k":"li","s":["follow advice from the local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information, including updates relating to airports and airspace which could close at short notice"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay away from areas around security or military facilities"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep your departure plans under review, noting that in April 2026 there was simultaneous closure of airspace and the King Fahd Causeway to Saudi Arabia, and ensure your travel documents are up to date"]},{"k":"li","s":["if advised to take shelter, stay indoors or find the nearest safe building or designated shelter. An interior stairwell or a room with as few external walls or windows as possible may provide additional protection. The greatest risk is from falling debris caused by intercepts, and you are safest inside a secure structure. Do not approach or touch any drone or missile fragments or unusual objects"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bahrain/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Bahrain’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Bahrain set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Bahrain Embassy in the UK","https://www.mofa.gov.bh/london/en/home/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Bahrain, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bahraini-UK dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dual nationality is generally not permitted under Bahraini law, unless formally agreed. If you hold both British and Bahraini nationalities, you will be considered a Bahraini national under local law during your stay in Bahrain. You should contact ",["Bahrain’s Nationality, Passports and Residency Affairs","https://www.npra.gov.bh/en/"]," (NPRA) to request approval of your dual citizenship status."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are a dual Bahraini-UK national the authorities may require you to enter and exit Bahrain on a Bahrain travel document only. If your Bahraini passport is not valid or in your possession, seek advice from your nearest Bahraini Embassy before you travel to Bahrain. Bahraini passport renewals whilst in Bahrain may take a long time and could potentially disrupt your travel plans. Decisions related to entering and exiting Bahrain are always made by the Bahraini authorities. ",["See who the FCDO can support abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/who-the-fcdo-can-support-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Bahrain Embassy in the UK","https://www.mofa.gov.bh/london/en/home/"]," or the ",["(NPRA)","https://www.npra.gov.bh/en/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to visit Bahrain."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can get a visa:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in advance online"]},{"k":"li","s":["in advance from the ",["Bahrain Embassy in the UK","https://www.mofa.gov.bh/london/en/visitiors-visas"]]},{"k":"li","s":["on arrival"]},{"k":"p","s":["Visas are automatically issued for a 2-week period, but visit visas for stays of up to 6 months are also available. You may be asked to provide evidence of onward or return travel when you apply."]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot start employment in Bahrain if you enter on a visit visa."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you overstay your visa, there could be penalties, legal issues and your work visa could be cancelled."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Extending visas"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can apply to renew your visa at the ",["Nationality, Passports and Residential Affairs department","https://www.npra.gov.bh/en/service-request/"]," at the Ministry of Interior."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for residency"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can apply for residency through the ",["Labour Market Regulatory Authority (LMRA)","https://lmra.gov.bh/en/home"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can be fined if you overstay your legal residency."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["You may be prevented from leaving Bahrain if you:"]},{"k":"li","s":["are subject to a travel ban"]},{"k":"li","s":["are involved in legal proceedings"]},{"k":"li","s":["have unpaid debt"]},{"k":"li","s":["are a child subject to a custody dispute"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re involved in a dispute, including civil and criminal disputes or immigration violation, you may be stopped from leaving the country. The travel ban will not be lifted until the issue is resolved. You may not know you’re subject to a travel ban until you try to leave or enter Bahrain. You can check with the ",["Bahrain Immigration Department","https://services.bahrain.bh/wps/portal/TravelBan_en"]," to see whether you’re subject to a travel ban."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Bahrain, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Bahrain guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/20/bahrain#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["As a public health measure, non-Bahraini passengers who have visited countries affected by the Ebola outbreak within the past 30 days will not be accepted for entry into the Kingdom of Bahrain. Check directly with local authorities and your airline before travel to confirm if this may apply to you."]},{"k":"p","s":["The World Health Organisation (WHO) has ",["declared this a Public Health Emergency of International Concern","https://www.who.int/news/item/17-05-2026-epidemic-of-ebola-disease-in-the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-and-uganda-determined-a-public-health-emergency-of-international-concern"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Bahrain","https://bahraincustoms.gov.bh/en/prohibited-and-declared"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Bahrain"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Bahrain."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreigners."]},{"k":"p","s":["Previous attacks using explosive devices in public places have killed and injured people. Such an attack has not been carried out successfully for several years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists have threatened to carry out attacks in the Gulf region, including on:"]},{"k":"li","s":["residential compounds"]},{"k":"li","s":["military, oil, transport and aviation interests"]},{"k":"li","s":["public places, including restaurants, hotels, beaches, shopping centres and mosques"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware of your surroundings, particularly during high profile events, and avoid large demonstrations."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Public gatherings, commemorations, demonstrations and protests take place. This can cause:"]},{"k":"li","s":["disruption to traffic and roadblocks"]},{"k":"li","s":["disturbances in villages and near economic centres"]},{"k":"li","s":["localised clashes between government security forces and protesters"]},{"k":"p","s":["The risk of protest can increase around anniversaries of significant events in Bahrain and can start with little warning. Locations of past protests include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Sitra"]},{"k":"li","s":["Bani Jamra"]},{"k":"li","s":["Karbabad"]},{"k":"li","s":["Saar"]},{"k":"li","s":["Karzakan"]},{"k":"li","s":["Budaiya Highway and surrounding villages"]},{"k":"li","s":["Diraz"]},{"k":"li","s":["Sanabis"]},{"k":"li","s":["Al Dair"]},{"k":"li","s":["Adliya"]},{"k":"li","s":["Nuwaidrait"]},{"k":"p","s":["Public gatherings in roads or public squares are temporarily banned to protect public safety. Leave the area if you see a large public gathering, demonstration or protest. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["remain vigilant"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the advice of the local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware of your surroundings"]},{"k":"li","s":["familiarise yourself with other routes in case you are diverted"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you see a suspect item, move away and call the police on 999 or the Police Hotline 8000 8008."]},{"k":"p","s":["Travel on the main routes during daylight hours is generally orderly. There can be a police presence or checkpoints on major roads."]},{"k":"p","s":["Political developments in the wider region have an impact on local public opinion and actions. Be aware of local sensitivities, follow news reports and be alert to local and regional developments, which could lead to public disturbances."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime is low in most areas, but you should take normal precautions to protect your belongings. For personal safety, only use reputable taxi companies."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bahrain is a liberal country compared to others in the region, but there are still conservative social views."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should respect local traditions, customs, laws and religions and make sure your actions do not cause offence, especially during Ramadan and other religious festivals. Bahrainis observe some religious anniversaries that may not be celebrated in other Gulf countries."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Security sites and incidents"]},{"k":"p","s":["Filming, photography, publishing or redistributing photos or videos of security and military sites, operations or incidents is prohibited. This includes the promotion of unverified or fabricated content pertaining to events, attacks or acts of aggression against Bahrain. Violation of this prohibition risks arrest and prosecution."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Social media"]},{"k":"p","s":["Respect the local culture and public security rules when using social media. It could amount to a crime if you post online any message, video or photograph, that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["is critical of the Bahrain government or monarchy"]},{"k":"li","s":["appears to abuse, ridicule or criticise the country"]},{"k":"li","s":["is culturally insensitive"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must carry photo ID such as a passport by law. You could be fined by the Bahraini authorities if you cannot show photo ID if asked."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dress conservatively in public places, particularly religious sites."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bahrainis often dress conservatively in traditional dress. You could cause offence if you dress inappropriately or not in accordance with Islamic values."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dress appropriately and modestly in public places, such as malls, restaurants, and parks. Clothing should not:"]},{"k":"li","s":["be transparent"]},{"k":"li","s":["expose shoulders or knees if you are a woman"]},{"k":"li","s":["display offensive pictures or slogans"]},{"k":"p","s":["Nudity is strictly forbidden, including topless sunbathing. These rules are even more closely observed during Ramadan when modesty is promoted."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Respect for religion"]},{"k":"p","s":["Islamic religious values are respected in Bahrain. Any disrespect towards religious beliefs or practices is considered deeply offensive and may lead to a heavy fine or a prison sentence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Muslims pray 5 times a day. Drivers may stop in lay-bys to pray."]},{"k":"p","s":["Other religions are respected in Bahrain and can be followed with freedom."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. During this time, do not:"]},{"k":"li","s":["eat, drink, smoke or chew gum in public in the daytime, including in your car"]},{"k":"li","s":["play loud music or dance"]},{"k":"li","s":["swear in public"]},{"k":"p","s":["These actions could amount to a crime under Bahraini law. Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that if hotels and restaurants are providing food or drink in fasting hours, they may separate you from Islamic guests, for example with screens"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local dress codes – clothing that does not meet local dress codes may cause more offence at this time"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that driving may be unpredictable, particularly when people are trying to get home at dusk"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that fasting can cause tiredness, particularly during the later afternoon and early evening"]},{"k":"li","s":["be patient and show tolerance"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public offences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Offensive language, spitting and aggressive behaviour (including ‘road rage’ hand gestures) are seen as seriously offensive and can result in a prison sentence and deportation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["Alcohol is legal in Bahrain. However, drunken public behaviour is against the law. You could be fined, imprisoned or deported. Physical assault and damaging public property is an offence, which may lead to a prison sentence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Security officers and airline staff will not tolerate passengers believed to be drunk at the airport, including those who are in transit. You may be denied boarding, detained and fined."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs are strictly forbidden, even a residual amount. Consuming or carrying illegal drugs, even if you are travelling through the airport, can lead to a prison sentence and deportation. Buying or selling illegal drugs and narcotics is illegal and can lead to a life sentence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some skincare products and e-cigarette refills may contain ingredients that are illegal in Bahrain, such as CBD oil."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drones and UAVs"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to fly drones or remote-controlled unmanned aerial vehicle flying devices without a valid licence or in restricted airspace. See the ",["Bahrain Civil Aviation Authority","https://www.bahrain.bh/wps/portal/en/BNP/AboutTheKingdom/Drones"]," for further details."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity between consenting adults who are at least 21 years old is not prohibited by law. However, same-sex couples showing affection in public may cause offence. You could be arrested under Bahrani law."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual relationships outside marriage"]},{"k":"p","s":["Consensual sexual activity between unmarried adults is not prohibited under Bahraini law. But there may be legal consequences if indecent acts happen in public. Sexual relations between a married person and someone other than their spouse may lead to legal consequences."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Unmarried couples sharing hotel accommodation"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no express prohibition or restriction under Bahraini law preventing unmarried couples from sharing hotel accommodation. However, some hotels may request proof of marriage. This would depend on the policy of each hotel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Bahrain, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Bahrain for up to 3 months. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are staying longer than 3 months, you’ll need to have the ",["1968 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," or ",["apply for a Bahraini driving licence","https://services.bahrain.bh/wps/portal/drivingschool_en"],". You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink-driving is a serious offence in Bahrain. If you are tested and found to have any alcohol in your system, you may get a fine, a travel ban, your driving licence withdrawn and a possible prison sentence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tailgating, speeding, racing, lane jumping and using a mobile phone while driving are all against the law and can result in heavy fines. Wearing seatbelts is mandatory. Failure to do so may result in your arrest or a fine."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a curfew on the waterways around Bahrain between 6.30pm to 4am."]},{"k":"p","s":["The local authorities are sensitive to the security around the sea areas of the Gulf. Vessels entering these waters or posts can be detained and inspected, and there have been occasional arrests. Make sure you have the necessary clearances before you enter the waters or visit ports. Avoid any sensitive areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when travelling by local sailing boats (‘dhows’). The safety of these vessels may not comply with UK standards. Make sure lifejackets are available."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 999 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Bahrain","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/20/bahrain#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See what ",["health risks you’ll face in Bahrain","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/20/bahrain"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are using prescribed drugs, you should carry a doctor’s note. If you plan to bring prescription drugs into Bahrain, you may need to seek prior agreement from the authorities. Check with the nearest Bahrain Embassy or consulate before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Bahrain"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Bahrain","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bahrain-list-of-medical-facilities-and-practitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be charged for emergency medical treatment. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],". See guidance on ",["mental health support for UK Nationals in Bahrain","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bahrain-mental-health-support-abroad/mental-health-support-for-uk-nationals-in-bahrain"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Air Quality"]},{"k":"p","s":["Poor outdoor air quality is a risk in the Kingdom of Bahrain. Read about the risks from ",["poor air quality on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/diseases/outdoor-air-quality"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can find more information and advice on air quality on the ",["World Health Organisation","https://www.who.int/health-topics/air-pollution#tab=tab_1"]," (WHO) website and check air quality levels on the ",["World Air Quality Index","https://aqicn.org/map/middleeast"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Bahrain"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 999 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Bahrain"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Bahrain"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Bahrain"]," in Bahrain"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Bahrain","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bahrain-bereavement-information-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Bahrain","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bahrain-prisoner-pack--2"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/bahrain/british-embassy-manama"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bahrain/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Bahrain","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-bahrain"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":20031,"change":"Updated information about regional tensions (See ‘Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/wainwright-fire-shows-the-importance-of-health-care-system-resilience-to-canadian-security-294715":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"6624e08347eb735c7c45e54cae2f6f4e033f668e1c2a9e215c6f2e7ed7848ea7","read":"https://theconversation.com/wainwright-fire-shows-the-importance-of-health-care-system-resilience-to-canadian-security-294715","bytes":185101,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Wainwright fire shows the importance of health-care system resilience to Canadian security","by":[{"n":"Bhavini Gohel","r":"Clinical Associate Professor, Cumming School of Medicine, University of Calgary"},{"n":"Marcia Clark","r":"Clinical professor, University of Calgary"}],"pub":"2026-10-20T14:09:10Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":[["The fire that swept through","https://www.canada.ca/en/department-national-defence/news/2026/10/incident-at-canadian-forces-base-wainwright.html"]," Canadian Forces Base Wainwright over the weekend in Alberta killed four soldiers and injured 39 people, including 19 reported in critical condition."]},{"k":"p","s":["The thoughts of Canadians are with the families, the military community, the people of Wainwright and the responders who answered the call."]},{"k":"p","s":["But ",["what happened after the fire","https://globalnews.ca/news/12107726/cfb-wainwright-timeline/"]," deserves attention too. Wainwright’s hospital became a triage hub for what the town’s mayor described as the largest mass casualty event the community has ever seen. Patients were also transferred to hospitals in Edmonton, Calgary and Red Deer. ",["The response mobilized 22 ground ambulances, six airplanes and two helicopters","https://apnews.com/article/1a41899da5b6e797b000061fa4da9c6a"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Canadian Armed Forces ",["relies on civilian systems for specialized services and mass casualty events","https://cimvhr.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/exercise-canada-paratus-post-exercise-report.pdf"],". Civilian health readiness is therefore part of national defence. Thirteen months before Wainwright, ",["Canada rehearsed the challenge of a casualty surge","https://cimvhr.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/exercise-canada-paratus-post-exercise-report.pdf"],". Its findings deserve action."]},{"k":"h","s":["A system with little slack"]},{"k":"p","s":["The response to a mass-casualty event does not play out in an otherwise empty health-care system. It competes with everyday care for staff, beds, transport and supplies."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Canadian Institute for Health Information (CIHI) ",["reports that hospital beds increased by only four per cent between 2014–15 and 2023–24","https://www.cihi.ca/en/spending-trends-in-health-service-delivery"]," as Canada’s population grew by 13 per cent. Beds per capita fell by seven per cent."]},{"k":"p","s":["These national figures don’t establish Alberta’s capacity on the day of the fire, but they show why having enough infrastructure, staff and expertise is so important."]},{"k":"p","s":["Alberta ",["has two burn centres, in Edmonton and Calgary","https://www.ameriburn.org/burn-care-team/resources/find-a-burn-center"],". That specialist capacity is an asset. But rural hospitals need staff, supplies and transportation to stabilize severely injured patients and move them safely to burn centres while continuing to serve their own communities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada’s health-care system sits at the centre of ",["what’s known as a polycrisis","https://www.stockholmresilience.org/research/research-stories/2025-08-19-the-dynamics-of-polycrisis-lessons-from-50-years-of-global-shocks.html"],": several systems are under strain, each situation compounding the other."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["‘Polycrisis’ may be a buzzword, but it could help us tackle the world’s woes","https://theconversation.com/polycrisis-may-be-a-buzzword-but-it-could-help-us-tackle-the-worlds-woes-195280"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Climate change is prolonging wildfire seasons. Inflation is squeezing budgets and supply chains. Workforce shortages are persisting after the ",["COVID-19 pandemic","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijdrr.2021.102325"],". The flu season is surging. The consequences of these crises affect health system response and care."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wainwright is experiencing its mass casualty event amid this ongoing polycrisis. The question is whether any system can absorb the next shock while still dealing with the last."]},{"k":"h","s":["What Canada already learned"]},{"k":"p","s":["In September 2025, 79 people from health-care systems across the country, federal agencies and the Canadian Armed Forces gathered in Toronto for ",["Exercise Canada Paratus","https://www.dlsph.utoronto.ca/2025/11/07/exercise-canada-paratus-post-exercise-report/"],". Paratus assessed overseas casualties, but the lessons apply to all hazards."]},{"k":"p","s":["Led by key disaster management teams and leaders, the exercise simulated about 100 casualties a week arriving in provincial and territorial health-care systems in Canada from a war in Europe. The post-exercise report is blunt. Three findings are relevant to planning after Wainwright:"]},{"k":"p","s":["• Capacity: The report identified workforce challenges and the need to expand infrastructure, staffing and expertise for sustained casualty surges."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Patient tracking: Canada has no integrated system to follow casualties as they move between military and civilian care. At Wainwright, the injured were dispersed across several hospitals within hours."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Governance: The report called for a federal–provincial–territorial health emergency and security authority with clear leadership, roles and decision rights. At the moment, there’s no organization co-ordinating health-care system capacity across federal, provincial and territorial governments."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health care is defence infrastructure"]},{"k":"p","s":["NATO already recognizes the link between healthcare and defence. One of its seven baseline requirements for national resilience ",["is the ability to manage mass casualties and disruptive health crises, including functioning civilian health systems and secure medical supplies","https://www.nato.int/en/what-we-do/deterrence-and-defence/resilience-civil-preparedness-and-article-3"],". Canada’s allies already treat health-care systems as strategic infrastructure, alongside energy grids and supply chains."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the ",["2025 Hague NATO summit","https://www.nato.int/en/about-us/official-texts-and-resources/official-texts/2025/06/25/the-hague-summit-declaration"],", allies agreed that up to 1.5 per cent of GDP within their new five per cent defence spending target could support resilience, including civil preparedness."]},{"k":"p","s":["Finland’s comprehensive security model ",["treats health security as a vital societal function","https://turvallisuuskomitea.fi/en/security-strategy-for-society/"],", while Sweden’s total defence approach ",["recognizes healthcare as essential to defence","https://government.se/press-releases/2025/09/new-package-for-stronger-civil-defence/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada should seize this opportunity to make a clear case for health investments that strengthen defence readiness."]},{"k":"h","s":["5 steps Canada must take"]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada already has the diagnosis. As the polycrisis deepens, sudden events like Wainwright will keep exposing the cost of failing to fill gaps. Here’s how Canada should respond:"]},{"k":"p","s":["First, implement the Paratus recommendations with a public timeline."]},{"k":"p","s":["Second, create the permanent federal–provincial–territorial health emergency body the report calls for."]},{"k":"p","s":["Third, build patient tracking that works across civilian and military care, so every casualty can be followed from the scene to recovery."]},{"k":"p","s":["Fourth, treat surge capacity, including rural hospitals near bases and critical infrastructure, as a defence-relevant investment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Finally, make the next national exercise a domestic, sudden scenario that applies a sudden mass-casualty event onto a system already under strain. New tools, including AI-enabled polycrisis simulation, allow authorities to rehearse these compounding scenarios before they happen; ",["they’re already being developed","https://obrieniph.ucalgary.ca/climate-health-system-alliance"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The clinicians and paramedics who responded at Wainwright were part of Canada’s defence capacity, regardless of whether we call them that."]},{"k":"p","s":["Paratus asked whether our health system could survive intact if war came to us from overseas. Wainwright answered a harder question: what happens when the emergency is already here."]},{"k":"p","s":["This article was co-authored by Stacey Litvinchuk, RN, MN, CHE, founder and CEO of Axiora Governance and former senior program officer for provincial surgery operations at Alberta Health Services."]}],"chars":6064},"https://theconversation.com/can-ethiopia-ever-be-at-peace-four-reasons-conflict-keeps-flaring-up-294278":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"a52ebce864cfa3abc670b094728161f33468ef46eec598f9e52f86f5b2738f6c","read":"https://theconversation.com/can-ethiopia-ever-be-at-peace-four-reasons-conflict-keeps-flaring-up-294278","bytes":184789,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Can Ethiopia ever be at peace? Four reasons conflict keeps flaring up","by":[{"n":"Alemayehu Fentaw Weldemariam","r":"Adjunct Professor and Ph.D. Fellow, Center for Constitutional Democracy, Indiana University"}],"pub":"2026-10-15T14:04:11Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Ethiopia has experienced ",["recurrent conflicts","https://www.cfr.org/global-conflict-tracker/conflict/conflict-ethiopia"]," for over five decades. This includes a long-running civil war sparked by the ",["overthrow of Emperor Haile Selassie","https://www.britannica.com/biography/Haile-Selassie-I"]," in 1974, ",["renewed fighting","https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-peace-deal-is-unravelling-what-went-wrong-with-the-tigray-agreement-293005"]," in Tigray, and ongoing conflicts in ",["Amhara","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cx2p8dpw1rwo"]," and ",["Oromia","https://ucdp.uu.se/conflict/413"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["renewed hostilities","https://www.chathamhouse.org/2026/10/war-has-returned-tigray-time-it-may-not-stay-ethiopia"]," in Tigray threaten to undo a peace process that had begun with an ",["agreement","https://igad.int/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/Download-the-signed-agreement-here.pdf"]," signed in Pretoria, South Africa, in 2022."]},{"k":"p","s":["Why has peace been so difficult to sustain in Ethiopia? My ",["research","https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&user=arlPf30AAAAJ&view_op=list_works&sortby=pubdate"]," on constitutional design and conflict points to four interconnected explanations:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the foundations of the Ethiopian state remain contested"]},{"k":"li","s":["ceasefires are mistaken for political settlements"]},{"k":"li","s":["armed force continues to be a route to political power"]},{"k":"li","s":["regional rivalries reinforce internal conflicts."]},{"k":"p","s":["The problem isn’t that Ethiopians of diverse ethnic backgrounds hate one another and can’t live together peacefully. It’s that successive political arrangements have failed to establish widely accepted rules for managing disagreements."]},{"k":"h","s":["1. The foundations of the state remain contested"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ethiopia’s ",["1995 constitution","https://constitutionnet.org/sites/default/files/Ethiopia_Constitution.pdf"]," emerged from a ",["political transition","https://www.history.com/this-day-in-history/may-28/ethiopian-capital-falls-to-rebels"]," that followed the overthrow of the military government in 1991. This ended ",["nearly two decades of civil war","https://www.ebsco.com/research-starters/history/military-junta-comes-power-ethiopia/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The new leadership sought to address long-standing grievances over ethnic marginalisation and demands for greater autonomy. It restructured the country as a ",["federation","https://theconversation.com/what-is-federalism-why-ethiopia-uses-this-system-of-government-and-why-its-not-perfect-217217"]," largely organised around ethnolinguistic communities. The constitution vested sovereignty in Ethiopia’s nations, nationalities and peoples. It guaranteed their ",["right to self-determination, including secession","https://www.ethiopianembassy.be/wp-content/uploads/Constitution-of-the-FDRE.pdf#page=13"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Proponents of federalism regard this right as ",["protection","https://www.jstor.org/stable/26557899"]," against historical domination. Opponents ",["argue","https://larc.cardozo.yu.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=2411&context=faculty-articles"]," that it entrenches ethnic boundaries and encourages ",["competition","https://www.africanews.com/2019/03/09/ethiopia-pm-moves-to-resolve-oromia-addis-ababa-boundary-rift/"]," over territory and ",["resources","https://reliefweb.int/report/ethiopia/what-s-driving-clashes-between-ethiopias-somali-oromia-regions"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ethnic diversity doesn’t inevitably lead to violence. And federalism isn’t inherently destabilising. It was introduced to accommodate competing national claims within a common political order."]},{"k":"p","s":["But constitutional recognition is not the same as political reconciliation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["What is federalism? Why Ethiopia uses this system of government and why it’s not perfect","https://theconversation.com/what-is-federalism-why-ethiopia-uses-this-system-of-government-and-why-its-not-perfect-217217"]]},{"k":"p","s":["The problem arises when a constitution sets out rules for sharing power and governing the country without sufficient agreement among the political groups expected to follow them. Instead of providing a common framework for resolving disputes, those rules become another source of political conflict."]},{"k":"h","s":["2. Ceasefires are mistaken for political settlements"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["2022 Pretoria agreement","https://igad.int/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/Download-the-signed-agreement-here.pdf"]," was about stopping hostilities, not about resolving their causes. The federal government and the Tigray People’s Liberation Front agreed to end two years of war. Major political questions were left for later negotiation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Disputed territories, regional administration, political participation and accountability for wartime abuses ",["remain contentious","https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-peace-deal-is-unravelling-what-went-wrong-with-the-tigray-agreement-293005"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Eritrea, a ",["major participant","https://theconversation.com/conflict-between-tigray-and-eritrea-the-long-standing-faultline-in-ethiopian-politics-151042"]," in the 2020-2022 war in Tigray, did not sign the agreement. Eritrean forces are still present in parts of Tigray."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Tigray People’s Liberation Front itself also became ",["fragmented","https://africa-eye.com/en/2026/08/09/tigrays-internal-divisions-reshape-the-balance-of-power-in-ethiopia/"]," after the war. Divisions emerged within the leadership. Disagreements over federal relations, political authority and control of military forces developed into a struggle within the movement."]},{"k":"p","s":["A peace agreement assumes that the parties signing it have ",["authority","https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/insurgent-fragmentation-in-the-horn-of-africa/141437F56565C561EA1996AE15FAA7C3"]," over their political and military organisations to honour their commitments. But when these organisations fragment, it becomes unclear who can carry out agreements."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Tigray leadership’s loss of legal party status ",["in 2025","https://addisstandard.com/ethiopias-election-board-revokes-tplfs-legal-status/"]," added another obstacle to political reintegration."]},{"k":"p","s":["These developments have undermined confidence that the transition from armed conflict to constitutional politics would be honoured."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Ethiopia’s peace deal is unravelling – what went wrong with the Tigray agreement","https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-peace-deal-is-unravelling-what-went-wrong-with-the-tigray-agreement-293005"]]},{"k":"p","s":["This distinction is fundamental. A cessation of hostilities can save lives immediately. But it cannot, by itself, establish a legitimate regional government, resolve territorial claims or restore trust between former enemies."]},{"k":"h","s":["3. Armed force is a route to political power"]},{"k":"p","s":["The use of violence to acquire or retain political authority has deep roots in Ethiopia’s modern history. In ",["1974","https://www.britannica.com/biography/Haile-Selassie-I"],", the military overthrew the empire-state and established a military regime. This regime was itself ",["overthrown in 1991","https://www.hrw.org/reports/1997/ethiopia/Ethio97d-02.htm"]," by a coalition of rebel forces led by the Ethiopian People’s Revolutionary Democratic Front."]},{"k":"p","s":["These transitions reinforced a pattern in which political power could be won through armed struggle. When political opponents have little confidence that elections, courts or negotiations can bring change, taking up arms can appear more effective than peaceful political competition."]},{"k":"p","s":["The continued use of force by both the state and armed groups makes this cycle ",["difficult to break","https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-national-dialogue-was-meant-to-heal-the-nation-but-divisions-are-deepening-278321"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Ethiopia’s national dialogue was meant to heal the nation, but divisions are deepening","https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-national-dialogue-was-meant-to-heal-the-nation-but-divisions-are-deepening-278321"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Abiy Ahmed became prime minister in ",["2018","https://medium.com/@ICTJ/ethiopias-transition-at-a-crossroad-4b418ece868c"]," after years of anti-government protests and divisions within the ruling coalition. Two years later, ",["rising political tensions","https://www.bbc.com/news/world-africa-54964378"]," led to war in Tigray. Abiy’s regime has ",["faced accusations","https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-amhara-crisis-abiys-political-failures-threaten-a-return-to-war-211754"]," of serious rights abuses and a lack of accountability."]},{"k":"p","s":["This has deepened distrust. It’s made ",["negotiated settlements","https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-national-dialogue-was-meant-to-heal-the-nation-but-divisions-are-deepening-278321"]," harder to achieve. Under Abiy, political authority has become increasingly personalised. Military operations and extraordinary security measures have been used to confront political challenges."]},{"k":"p","s":["Peace needs a political environment where losing an election doesn’t mean exclusion from power or exposure to coercion."]},{"k":"h","s":["4. Regional rivalries reinforce internal conflicts"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ethiopia’s domestic conflicts are increasingly intersecting with the interests and actions of neighbouring countries. Eritrean forces ",["fought beside","https://theconversation.com/eritrea-is-involved-in-tigray-to-boost-its-stature-why-the-strategy-could-backfire-175591"]," Ethiopia’s army in Tigray. They remained in parts of the region after the 2022 peace deal. Now the former allies are ",["adversaries","https://theconversation.com/ethiopia-and-eritrea-are-on-edge-again-whats-behind-the-growing-risk-of-war-276424"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been accusations of ",["cross-border military intervention","https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/ethiopian-troops-enter-town-border-with-eritrea-stoking-war-fears-2026-10-13/"],". This has renewed concerns that the war in Tigray could develop into a wider conflict."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ethiopia’s ambitions to ",["secure Red Sea access","https://theconversation.com/ethiopia-eritrea-tensions-over-red-sea-port-have-turned-the-tigray-peace-deal-into-a-political-weapon-290096"]," have further complicated relations with Eritrea and Somalia. Its ",["2024 agreement","https://theconversation.com/somaliland-ethiopia-port-deal-international-opposition-flags-complex-red-sea-politics-221131"]," with Somaliland provoked a dispute with Mogadishu."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ethiopia also has strained relations with Egypt over its ",["mega dam in the Nile River","https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-mega-dam-has-taken-14-years-to-build-what-it-means-for-the-niles-11-river-states-and-why-its-so-controversial-264665"],". Sudan’s ",["ongoing civil war","https://www.cfr.org/global-conflict-tracker/conflict/power-struggle-sudan"]," and rival Saudi Arabia and Emirati relationships across the Red Sea ",["add further pressures","https://theconversation.com/middle-eastern-monarchies-in-sudans-war-whats-driving-their-interests-251825"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Ethiopia and Eritrea are on edge again: what’s behind the growing risk of war","https://theconversation.com/ethiopia-and-eritrea-are-on-edge-again-whats-behind-the-growing-risk-of-war-276424"]]},{"k":"p","s":["These external tensions can make domestic troubles harder to contain. Ethiopia has a duty to defend its boundaries and also to respect those of its neighbours."]},{"k":"h","s":["What would lasting peace require?"]},{"k":"p","s":["These four obstacles to peace reinforce one another:"]},{"k":"li","s":["disagreements over constitutional rules fuel political tensions"]},{"k":"li","s":["armed conflict makes inclusive negotiations more difficult"]},{"k":"li","s":["peace agreements that fail to address underlying grievances leave the door open to renewed violence"]},{"k":"li","s":["competing regional interests complicate efforts to achieve lasting peace."]},{"k":"p","s":["As a result, Ethiopia’s recurring conflicts cannot be resolved through ceasefires alone."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lasting peace requires all Ethiopians to agree on how power is shared, and the relationship between the federal government and its regions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["What makes peace talks successful? The 4 factors that matter","https://theconversation.com/what-makes-peace-talks-successful-the-4-factors-that-matter-206299"]]},{"k":"p","s":["But resolving Ethiopia’s internal divisions will not, on its own, settle tensions with neighbouring countries. That requires diplomacy built on respect for sovereignty, non-interference and peaceful negotiation over interests."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ethiopia therefore faces two interconnected challenges. First, building a political system that its diverse communities can accept. Second, establishing peaceful relations with its neighbours."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lasting peace depends on both."]}],"chars":7771},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/oman":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-20T17:20Z","sha":"30ae1de037c65a976a2e8ae28a03add1b2345189bb27dcd92d48a6af9a297105","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/oman","bytes":74144,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Oman travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-29T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-18T16:31:54+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional tensions"]},{"k":"p","s":["The context in the Middle East remains deeply unpredictable and the risk of sudden escalation is high. Since conflict began in early 2026, Iran has stated its intention to target locations associated with the US and Israel, including, but not limited to, organisations, businesses, facilities, and institutions. There have been strikes and retaliatory attacks by Iran and others across the region against civilian and military infrastructure. There remains a risk of further attacks across the region at short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals in, or planning to travel through, the Middle East should be prepared for possible flight cancellations, airspace closures, and travel disruptions. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["read ",["If you’re affected by a crisis abroad - GOV.UK","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],". This includes guidance on “how to prepare for a crisis” with suggestions on what you might include in your emergency supplies and “what to do in a crisis”"]},{"k":"li","s":["sign up to FCDO Travel Advice ",["email alerts","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/oman/email-signup"]]},{"k":"li","s":["follow advice from the local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information, including updates relating to airports and airspace which could close at short notice"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay away from areas around security or military facilities"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep your departure plans under review, and ensure your travel documents are up to date"]},{"k":"li","s":["if advised to take shelter, stay indoors or find the nearest safe building or designated shelter. An interior stairwell or a room with as few external walls or windows as possible may provide additional protection. The greatest risk is from falling debris caused by intercepts, and you are safest inside a secure structure. Do not approach or touch any drone or missile fragments or unusual objects"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/oman/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Oman’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Oman set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Omani Embassy in the UK","https://www.fm.gov.om/london/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Oman, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["British-Omani dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["Oman does not recognise dual nationality. If you hold both British and Omani passports, the Omani authorities may confiscate one of your passports."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Oman for up to 14 days without a visa."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you overstay or do not extend your visa or residency, the Omani authorities may fine and detain you. Fines can be up to 10 Omani rials a day, with a total maximum fine of 500 rials."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer than 14 days or for work, study or other reasons, you must have a visa. To avoid the risk of refusal, it’s better to ",["apply for a visa online","https://evisa.rop.gov.om/"]," before you travel – you can select the ‘unsponsored visit visa’ option if you’re a tourist."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also get a visit visa on arrival at an airport in Oman."]},{"k":"h","s":["Checks at border control"]},{"k":"p","s":["At Omani border control, you must be able to show:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a ticket for return or onward travel"]},{"k":"li","s":["proof of your accommodation – for example, a hotel booking"]},{"k":"li","s":["proof of your travel health insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from Rwanda, Tanzania or a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Oman guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/170/oman#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Oman","https://www.customs.gov.om/en"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking medicines into Oman"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some UK prescription and over-the-counter medicines are illegal in Oman. Carry a copy of your prescription if you’re bringing medicine. Check with ",["Oman’s Ministry of Health","https://www.moh.gov.om/en/-/---276"]," well before you travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Oman"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Oman cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate including in places visited by foreigners."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists have threatened to carry out attacks in the Gulf region, including on:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Residential compounds"]},{"k":"li","s":["Military, oil, transport and aviation interests"]},{"k":"li","s":["Public places, including restaurants, hotels, beaches, shopping centres and places of worship"]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports, including official messaging from ",["Oman’s Government Communication Centre","https://x.com/Oman_GC"],", and follow the advice of the local authorities, including the ",["Royal Oman Police","https://www.rop.gov.om/english/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Examples of significant incidents include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in July 2024, 6 people were killed and others injured in a shooting incident in the vicinity of a mosque, in the Wadi Kabir area of Muscat."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Developments in the Middle East continue to affect public opinion in Oman. In October 2023, there was a small, peaceful demonstration outside the British Embassy. Further unannounced demonstrations are possible throughout the country. Stay alert and avoid large crowds."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware of local sensitivities on these issues and follow the advice of the Omani authorities, including the ",["Royal Oman Police","https://www.rop.gov.om/english/"],". Follow news reports and be alert to local and regional developments, which might trigger public disturbances."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Personal attacks against foreign nationals, including sexual assault and rape, are relatively rare, but happen. Take care when walking or travelling alone, particularly at night. You should maintain at least the same level of personal security awareness as you would in the UK. See ",["advice for women travelling abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Oman’s laws and customs are very different to those in the UK and reflect the fact that Oman is an Islamic country. You should respect local traditions, customs, laws and religions at all times. Make sure your actions do not offend, especially during the holy month of Ramadan or if you plan to visit religious areas."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry a copy of the photo page of your passport and keep the original in a safe place. If you live in Oman, carry your Omani ID."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. During this time, do not:"]},{"k":"li","s":["eat, drink, smoke or chew gum in public in the daytime, including in your car"]},{"k":"li","s":["play loud music or dance"]},{"k":"li","s":["swear in public"]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that if hotels and restaurants are providing food or drink in fasting hours, they may separate you from Islamic guests, for example with screens"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local dress codes – clothing that does not meet local dress codes may cause more offence at this time"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that fasting can cause tiredness, particularly during the later afternoon and early evening"]},{"k":"li","s":["be patient and show tolerance"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourists and visitors can buy and drink alcohol in licensed venues, such as hotels, restaurants and clubs. The legal drinking age is 21."]},{"k":"p","s":["Non-Muslim residents can get a licence to drink alcohol at home from the Royal Oman Police. Liquor licences are not available to non-residents."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to drink alcohol in public, be drunk in public or to drink-drive. The police have arrested and charged British nationals for these offences. Border police may arrest passengers travelling through Omani airports or seaports under the influence of alcohol."]},{"k":"hs","s":["E-cigarette and vape bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to import or use e-cigarettes or vape products in Oman."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Blood test following arrest"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are arrested, the authorities may require you to take a blood test, particularly if they suspect you have used drugs or alcohol. If you refuse, you could be arrested for your failure to comply."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress codes"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should dress modestly in public areas including in shopping malls. Your clothing should cover the tops of your arms and legs (below the knee), and underwear should not be visible."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wearing tight-fitting clothes is likely to attract attention. Do not wear swimming costumes or beachwear in public areas, except on tourist beaches or at swimming pools."]},{"k":"p","s":["Cross-dressing is illegal."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Unmarried couples"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to live with or share a hotel room with someone of the opposite sex if you are not married or closely related."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may have difficulty registering the birth of a baby born in Oman if you are unmarried or in a relationship the Omani authorities do not recognise as marriage."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs penalties"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are severe penalties for importing, trafficking, smuggling and possessing drugs, even residual amounts. In some cases, offenders could get the death penalty. There is no distinction in Omani law between ‘soft’ and ‘hard’ drugs – both are treated with equal severity."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public offences"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to swear and make rude gestures, including while driving. You can also be charged with obscenity for social media posts or shared photos or videos."]},{"k":"p","s":["Showing affection in public is frowned upon and may bring you to the attention of the police."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pornography"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to create, import or share pornographic images and videos, even if created for personal use with the consent of those involved."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras and binoculars"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to photograph some government buildings and military sites. Do not photograph people without their permission. Hobbies like bird watching and plane spotting may be misunderstood – particularly near military sites, government buildings and airports."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drones"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to fly drones or any other remote-controlled flying device without a valid licence or in restricted airspace."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is illegal in Oman. Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Financial crimes and unpaid bills"]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals must pay all debts and traffic fines before leaving Oman. You can check if you have outstanding traffic fines via the ROP app or online service: ",["Royal Oman Police Website - Online Services - Traffic Offense Payment","https://www.rop.gov.om/OnlineServices/eTraffic/english/default.aspx"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Financial crimes and unpaid bills include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["fraud"]},{"k":"li","s":["giving somebody a cheque which bounces (including post-dated and ‘security’ cheques)"]},{"k":"li","s":["non-payment of bills (for example property rent, hotel bills or car hire)"]},{"k":"p","s":["You may also be liable for cheques that you have signed on behalf of a company."]},{"k":"p","s":["Financial crimes can be punished with:"]},{"k":"li","s":["imprisonment"]},{"k":"li","s":["fines"]},{"k":"li","s":["deportation"]},{"k":"li","s":["freezing bank accounts and other assets"]},{"k":"li","s":["seizing of any end-of-service benefits or bonuses"]},{"k":"li","s":["blocking your access to possible future sponsors (employers)"]},{"k":"li","s":["delay and/or prevention from leaving the country"]},{"k":"p","s":["See more details about ",["financial crimes if you are living and working in Oman.","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-oman--2"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Child custody cases"]},{"k":"p","s":["The border authorities may prevent children from leaving Oman if they are the subject of a child custody dispute."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiking and mountaineering"]},{"k":"p","s":["When hiking in Oman, be sure to follow marked hiking trails."]},{"k":"p","s":["Extreme heat has caused deaths in Oman due to dehydration and heat exhaustion – see ",["advice for travellers affected by extreme heat","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/news/632/heatwaves"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Oman, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive a rental car in Oman for the first 6 weeks after you arrive. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["1949 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you live in Oman or are staying longer than 6 weeks, you must get an Omani licence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience, a higher minimum age and holding an IDP."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink-driving is a serious offence in Oman. If you are tested and found to have any alcohol in your system, you may get a fine and possible imprisonment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Reporting traffic accidents"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are involved in a serious traffic accident and do not need emergency treatment, you must stay with your vehicle and call the Royal Oman Police on 9999."]},{"k":"p","s":["Serious accidents include those with:"]},{"k":"li","s":["severe damage to vehicles"]},{"k":"li","s":["injuries or deaths"]},{"k":"li","s":["damage to public or private property"]},{"k":"li","s":["drink-driving or drugs"]},{"k":"li","s":["one or more drivers without a licence (or with a suspended licence)"]},{"k":"li","s":["uninsured vehicles"]},{"k":"li","s":["military or security vehicles"]},{"k":"p","s":["You may not need to call the police after a minor accident, but you must complete a minor road traffic accident form. You must keep a form in your car – you can get one from your insurance company and at a police station. Car rental companies are responsible for keeping forms in their cars."]},{"k":"p","s":["In a minor accident there is generally:"]},{"k":"li","s":["limited damage to vehicles"]},{"k":"li","s":["no injury or death"]},{"k":"li","s":["no damage to public or private property, apart from vehicles and property belonging to those involved"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rules of the road"]},{"k":"p","s":["Rules of the road in Oman include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["all passengers must wear seatbelts"]},{"k":"li","s":["all children aged 3 and under must use child car seats"]},{"k":"li","s":["it is illegal to use a mobile phone while driving"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Omani authorities strictly enforce traffic laws. There are severe penalties for traffic offences, including fines of up to 3,000 Omani rials or prison sentences of up to 3 years."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving can be dangerous outside Muscat. There is a risk of hitting wandering camels and goats on the road. Rainfall can cause sudden, severe floods in dry riverbeds and on roads that cross them."]},{"k":"p","s":["The condition of Omani roads is generally good. Driving standards in Oman are not always as disciplined as those in the UK, and the rate of traffic accidents in Oman is significantly higher."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Desert and mountain travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Road trips to the desert and mountains can be dangerous unless you’re in a well-equipped 4-wheel-drive vehicle. You should always:"]},{"k":"li","s":["travel in convoy if possible"]},{"k":"li","s":["take a supply of water"]},{"k":"li","s":["take a mobile phone or satellite phone"]},{"k":"li","s":["leave a copy of your travel plans with friends or relatives"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure you’re insured for this type of travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The safety of tourist boats may not be up to UK standards. Make sure life jackets are available for all passengers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many areas of the Gulf of Aden are restricted. Vessels entering these areas have been detained and inspected, sometimes resulting in arrests. You should make careful enquiries before entering these waters or visiting ports. Consider how regional tensions may affect your route."]},{"k":"p","s":["Vessels may be at increased risk of maritime attack, including piracy, in:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Gulf of Oman"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Northern Arabian Sea"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Gulf of Aden"]},{"k":"li","s":["Bab El Mandeb"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["piracy in the Gulf of Aden and Indian Ocean","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"],". The threat assessment of the combined international naval counter-piracy forces is that sailing yachts should not enter the ",["designated high-risk area","https://on-shore.mschoa.org/"],", due to the risk of hijacking."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tropical cyclones"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tropical cyclones from the Indian Ocean sometimes affect Oman in July and August, disrupting services and utilities."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow official weather warnings"]},{"k":"li","s":["check local weather forecasts, weathers warnings from Oman’s ",["civil aviation authority","https://www.caa.gov.om/en"]," and the ",["World Meteorological Organization reports for Oman","https://severeweather.wmo.int/tc/in/"]]},{"k":"li","s":["get advice about travelling conditions, particularly if you’re planning off-road travel or adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flash floods"]},{"k":"p","s":["Flash floods can cause injuries and deaths. Wadis (dry riverbeds) in Oman are prone to flash flooding after heavy rainfall from October to March."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before travelling to a wadi, check the weather forecast and avoid places where heavy rain is expected and for at least one day afterwards."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re caught in a flash flood:"]},{"k":"li","s":["go to a high point"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not try to cross the water"]},{"k":"li","s":["drive to a dry spot if you’re in a vehicle"]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow any instructions or guidance from the Royal Oman Police and the ",["Civil Defence & Ambulance Authority","https://cdaa.gov.om/"],".bYou can also use the Nidaa/CDAA to stay up to date with any emergency updates."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 9999 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Oman","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/170/oman#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Oman","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/170/oman#General_Information"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["Middle East respiratory syndrome coronavirus"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Oman. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Extreme heat has caused deaths in Oman due to dehydration and heat exhaustion."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Oman"]},{"k":"p","s":["The quality of healthcare facilities in Oman is similar to those in the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals must use the private healthcare system. Visitors who do not have travel insurance or the means to settle any charges may be stopped from leaving the country until the debt is paid. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Oman","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/oman-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Oman","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-oman--2"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Oman"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 9999 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Oman"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Oman"]," in Oman"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Oman","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-information-for-oman"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Oman","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/oman-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/oman/british-embassy-muscat"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/oman/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Oman","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-oman"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":21155,"change":"Updated information about regional tensions (See ‘Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/turkmenistan":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"7af597f68d9c179c93a2133581d4db14222931490bb5c47f4f47e2daca35eed5","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/turkmenistan","bytes":57322,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Turkmenistan travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-07T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-10-21T15:50:49+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East. Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator before travelling"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy for coverage before you travel"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information and sign up for travel advice email alerts"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and get ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/turkmenistan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Turkmenistan’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Turkmenistan set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Embassy of Turkmenistan in the UK","https://uk.tmembassy.gov.tm/en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Entering Turkmenistan across the land border from Iran"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are a British national wanting to enter Turkmenistan from Iran, you will need special authorisation from the Government of Turkmenistan and confirmation of an onward flight."]},{"k":"p","s":["Authorisation can be facilitated by the British Embassy in Ashgabat by ",["contacting the FCDO","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/home"]," before you travel to the border, indicating whether you are contacting from Iran or from the UK on behalf of a relative."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will need to provide personal details (name, date of birth, passport information) of the person travelling and a copy of an onward flight reservation, and indicate which border crossing they intend to use. The authorisation process will likely take about 48 hours but may be longer. Normal visa fees of 70-100 US dollars will be applied on arrival in Turkmenistan and must be paid in cash."]},{"k":"p","s":["Access to the internet and mobile phone networks is restricted in Turkmenistan. If you intend to leave Iran overland, you do so at your own risk. In Iran, holding a British passport or having perceived connections to the UK can be reason enough for the Iranian authorities to detain you."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more FCDO advice ",["if you’re affected by a crisis abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["COVID-19 rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["All travellers entering Turkmenistan must undergo a COVID-19 test upon arrival, which costs 31 US dollars cash."]},{"k":"p","s":["Confirm the latest requirements with your Turkmen sponsor."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Turkmenistan, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you plan to leave Turkmenistan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to visit Turkmenistan."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have the wrong visa or if you overstay your visa, you could be prosecuted and possibly imprisoned."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 1 October 2026 Turkmenistan introduced an electronic (e-visa) system for tourists and people visiting to participate in international conferences and exhibitions backed by the Government of Turkmenistan."]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot apply for one of these visas directly. Your tour agency or event organiser will continue to act as a sponsor. However, when the visa is approved and paid for through your sponsor, you will receive an e-visa that can be printed off or presented electronically on arrival. The e-visa replaces the former two-part process of a letter of invitation followed by a visa vignette in your passport."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to visit Turkmenistan for any purpose other than tourism or conference participation, you continue to need a letter of invitation applied for on your behalf by a sponsoring organisation. Once you have the letter of invitation you can apply for your visa either at your nearest Embassy of Turkmenistan or on arrival."]},{"k":"p","s":["The cost of any visa is dependent on your length of stay in Turkmenistan and whether you are applying for a single or multiple entry visa. The website of ",["Turkmenistan’s State Migration Service","https://migration.gov.tm/"]," has more information about visas and border requirements."]},{"k":"p","s":["For visas needing to follow the letter of invitation process, Visas applications through an Embassy of Turkmenistan are referred to Ashgabat for a decision, which can take up to a month unless a paid-for express service is available. Visas on arrival attract an additional fee of 50 US dollars."]},{"k":"p","s":[["The website of the Embassy of Turkmenistan","https://uk.tmembassy.gov.tm/en/consular-services/visa-info"]," in London includes a Visa Fees table for applications submitted to the Embassy."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Transit visas and travelling through Turkmenistan by car"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you will be travelling overland through Turkmenistan territory for fewer than 5 days, and the purpose of your stay is the transit rather than tourism, you may be eligible for a transit visa."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Turkmen State Migration Service is the sole sponsor of transit visas."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must secure the letter of invitation before you travel, and it can take up to a month for a letter of invitation to issue. This can then be converted to a transit visa at the land border checkpoint."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["website of the Embassy of Turkmenistan in London","https://uk.tmembassy.gov.tm/en/consular-services/visa-info"]," sets out the eligibility criteria for a transit visa. You cannot change your transit visa to a tourist visa, and you must enter and leave Turkmenistan using the border crossings specified in the letter of invitation."]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot buy a transit visa for Turkmenistan at Baku seaport. You must secure it ahead of time."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be charged up to 150 US dollars to bring a car into Turkmenistan by land or sea."]},{"k":"p","s":["A transit visa is not needed for layover flights where you will remain airside. You should contact the ",["Embassy of Turkmenistan in London","https://uk.tmembassy.gov.tm/en/"]," or your airline with further questions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Border officials may close Turkmen border crossings without notice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Turkmenistan guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/228/turkmenistan#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Registering with the authorities"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re staying in the country for more than 3 working days, you must register with the State Migration Service of Turkmenistan within 3 days of your arrival. Your hotel or sponsor will usually register you. Confirm this with them before you travel, including what documentation is required."]},{"k":"p","s":["To register, you will usually need:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your passport"]},{"k":"li","s":["2 passport-size photos, and"]},{"k":"li","s":["written confirmation of where you are staying from your sponsor"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxes for foreign nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["On arrival, you must pay a migration fee of 14 US dollars. All foreign visitors must also pay a ‘tourism tax’ of 2 US dollars for each day of their stay in Turkmenistan. Hotels include the tax as a separate item on your bill."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may be charged additional taxes on entry. Bring enough cash (US dollars) to cover unexpected charges."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Turkmenistan","https://customs.gov.tm/en/customs-info/for-individuals"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["‘Tobacco products to the amount of 2 packs’ means you can bring one of:"]},{"k":"li","s":["2 packets of cigarettes – a total of 40 cigarettes"]},{"k":"li","s":["2 cigars"]},{"k":"li","s":["2 packs of tobacco each weighing no more than a packet of cigarettes"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to give tobacco products as a gift. If you are caught, you could get a fine."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Turkmenistan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Turkmenistan is largely a cash-based society. Carry cash and pay in the Turkmen currency, manat. Some larger hotels and restaurants accept US dollars - you should check before purchasing. Other outlets are only allowed to accept manat."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can exchange US dollars at the official manat rate at your hotel or a bank. Bring crisp, clean notes as creased, damaged or marked notes will be rejected. Notes issued before 2013 may also be rejected. 100 US dollar bills with the blue ribbon are favoured over the older white and green notes. You can check which version of dollar notes you have on the ",["US government website","https://www.uscurrency.gov/denominations/100"],". Other currencies are difficult to exchange. Manat cannot be re-converted, so exchange only as much as you need."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is possible in Ashgabat to use a UK bank card to withdraw manat from an ATM or buy manat over the counter, but only at the State Bank for Foreign Economic Affairs. There’s a 3% withdrawal charge for each transaction. You are strongly recommended to bring enough dollars for your entire trip."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Turkmenistan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Turkmenistan, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Border restrictions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Turkmen land border crossings can be subject to occasional and unannounced closures. The borders with Afghanistan and Iran are particularly sensitive, with access to areas near these borders being tightly restricted."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police sometimes carry out checks of identity documents. Always carry your passport on you. Keep a copy of the photo page of your passport and your letter of invitation in a safe place."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Whilst the crime rate is low, you should exercise a similar level of caution as you would in the UK."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. Cafés and restaurants may amend their menus and be busy around fast-breaking (‘Iftar’). Areas around mosques are also likely to be busy around prayer times. Take particular care not to offend religious sensitivities at this time."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to drink alcohol in any communal spaces, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["parks or public squares"]},{"k":"li","s":["forests or beaches"]},{"k":"li","s":["train stations, airports or sea ports"]},{"k":"li","s":["underpasses"]},{"k":"li","s":["government offices"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re caught drinking alcohol in these places you can get a fine of 100 manats."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Smoking and e-cigarette bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to smoke outside or in any communal spaces unless they contain a designated smoking area."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re found guilty of possession or use of illegal drugs, you could face a lengthy prison sentence in very basic conditions."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking photos in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to take pictures of certain buildings. Check before taking photos of or near airports, military infrastructure, police stations, government buildings or embassies. The guards at the presidential palace may tell you not to take photos of it."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Turkmen can be sensitive about having their picture taken without their consent."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Internet and mobile network"]},{"k":"p","s":["Internet connections outside the larger hotels can be unreliable. Many social media apps and websites are blocked, including YouTube, X, Facebook and WhatsApp. Access to Yahoo, Gmail and Hotmail is often difficult. VPNs are illegal in Turkmenistan and are usually blocked as soon as the authorities identify them."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a single state-owned mobile telephone provider, Altyn Asyr, which uses the TM CELL brand. Altyn Asyr does not provide a roaming service and the quality of the network is low."]},{"k":"p","s":["Comments, including content posted on social media, interpreted as being negative about Turkmenistan’s political system and traditions are taken very seriously and may constitute an offence. Many Turkmen are uncomfortable discussing politics."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to take pictures of certain buildings. Ask before taking pictures of anything of possible military or security interest, including government buildings and food markets."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Relationships with Turkmens"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal for a Turkmen woman to have a sexual relationship with a foreign national. Foreign nationals who provide gifts, transport or other benefits to women in expectation of even a short relationship can be immediately fined and deported."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Male same-sex sexual activity is illegal, and punishable by a prison sentence. Same-sex relationships generally meet with disapproval in Turkmen society. Avoid showing affection in public."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive a hire car or a UK vehicle, see information on ",["driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to have both the ",["1968 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards are poor. Road travel at night outside cities is particularly dangerous because of the condition of the roads. There is a 60km/h speed limit in much of Ashgabat, enforced by both static speed cameras and police with mobile speed cameras. There are no signs warning of speed cameras."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Licensed taxis are clearly identified by white and green markings. Avoid unlicensed taxis."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although taxis have meters, drivers will usually charge foreign nationals around 20 manat for a journey within the city centre. They might ask for payment in US dollars, but this is illegal. Most taxi drivers do not speak much English."]},{"k":"p","s":["Licensed taxis are also available from Exit 2 of Ashgabat International Airport (outside Exit 2 of the terminal), although you should agree a price before getting in. Receipts are rarely provided. Alternatively, most upmarket hotels can arrange airport transfers. Email them in advance to make arrangements or ask at the front desk."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Turkmenistan is in an active seismic zone. There are regular tremors and there have been strong earthquakes."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency has advice about what to do before, during and after an earthquake."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 03 from a landline or 003 from a mobile and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Turkmenistan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/228/turkmenistan#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Turkmenistan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/228/turkmenistan"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Air quality in cities in Turkmenistan can deteriorate from time to time. Minimise your exposure by staying indoors in an air-conditioned environment. Wash all fruit, vegetables and other foods that might have been exposed, and regularly damp-dust indoor surfaces."]},{"k":"p","s":["Typhoid and hepatitis A are endemic. You should drink or use only boiled and filtered or bottled water and avoid ice in drinks."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the summer temperatures regularly reach 45°C in the shade, so drink plenty of water in the summer and avoid sunburn."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["Turkmenistan’s State Customs Service report that individuals may enter Turkmenistan with prescription medicines providing they have a copy of the prescription with the medicine. There is no requirement to declare the medicine. Before travelling check with your tour company and the ",["State Customs Service","https://customs.gov.tm/en/customs-info/for-individuals"]," for the latest regulations."]},{"k":"p","s":["You could be prosecuted for possession of some drugs that Turkmenistan may classify as narcotics, such as morphine or even strong painkillers, if you do not have a prescription, or if you’re carrying more than you need for your visit and do not declare them on arrival."]},{"k":"p","s":["TravelHealthPro explains ",["best practice when travelling with medicines","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Turkmenistan"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no reciprocal healthcare agreement between the UK and Turkmenistan."]},{"k":"p","s":["The quality of medical care is poor, and it is a lot more expensive than in the UK. Anything other than basic or emergency treatment, particularly outside Ashgabat, is usually best avoided. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Turkmenistan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners-in-turkmenistan"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Turkmenistan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance:"]},{"k":"li","s":["03 from landline"]},{"k":"li","s":["003 from mobile"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire:"]},{"k":"li","s":["01 from landline"]},{"k":"li","s":["001 from mobile"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police:"]},{"k":"li","s":["02 from landline"]},{"k":"li","s":["002 from mobile"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Turkmenistan"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Turkmenistan"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Turkmenistan"]]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Turkmenistan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/turkmenistan-bereavement-death-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Turkmenistan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/turkmenistan-prisoners-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/turkmenistan/british-embassy-ashgabat"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/turkmenistan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Turkmenistan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-turkmenistan"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":19443,"change":"Updated information about COVID-19 rules, applying for visas, transit visas and taking cash into Turkmenistan (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/epic-blue-wave-helps-democrats-take-congress-in-overwhelming-rebuke-to-president-trump-295830":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"84ea49c9a7ce4f5cd4cefb561b3ae196fab1edb086c35444b304c41a3d5b4b11","read":"https://theconversation.com/epic-blue-wave-helps-democrats-take-congress-in-overwhelming-rebuke-to-president-trump-295830","bytes":184183,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"‘Epic’ blue wave helps Democrats take Congress in overwhelming rebuke to President Trump","by":[{"n":"Charlie Hunt","r":"Associate Professor of Political Science, Boise State University"}],"pub":"2026-11-04T05:48:52Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Voters turned out in ",["massive numbers on Election Day","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/03/us/election-day-turnout-battleground-states.html"]," to hand Democrats control of Congress, in a sweeping snub of President Donald Trump and Republicans. ",["Democrats won several statewide races in places long considered GOP bastions","https://www.wired.com/story/democrats-sweep-republicans-in-nearly-every-race-that-matters/"],", including races that were ",["considered insurmountable even weeks ago","https://www.washingtonpost.com/elections/results/2026/11/03/south-carolina-senate-live-updates/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Democrats took control of the House and Senate","https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/11/03/us/midterms-2026-election-day-trump"],", flipping Senate seats in ",["Texas","https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-elections/texas-senate-results"],", South Carolina, North Carolina, ",["Kansas","https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/6182761-democrat-adam-hamilton-flips-kansas-senate-seat-2026-midterms/"]," and Ohio. The results reflected broad dissatisfaction across the country with Trump, his agenda and the candidates he had endorsed."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Conversation’s senior politics editor, Alfonso Serrano, spoke on election night with Charlie Hunt, ",["a scholar at Boise State University who studies Congress and elections","https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=FeSk64QAAAAJ&hl=en"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["It was obviously a strong showing for Democrats on Election Day, something that was even evident in the margin of some Democratic losses. What does it tell you, for example, that democratic socialist Angie Nixon fought a competitive race for the Senate in Florida?"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is this big uniform shift toward the Democrats that we’re seeing really across virtually all kinds of locations and geographies and counties. What I think is particularly notable here, and something we were on the lookout for in this election, and we’re seeing it, is the ",["substantial shift in the Hispanic vote","https://www.cbsnews.com/news/texas-democrats-hispanic-vote-midterms-talarico-paxton-hinojosa-abbott/"]," from 2024 in places like Texas and Florida, where you’re getting these 30-to-35 point shifts from how Donald Trump performed in 2024. That was ",["a big part of what helped him win","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cmwyqn6ejyd4o"],", and it seems like it has snapped right back and even farther in the other direction. This is what made Florida, I think, closer than a lot of folks thought."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s what put a number of really, really right-leaning districts in play, particularly in South Florida. And it looks like it is going to help Democrats keep the number of seats they had in Florida in the House that they had before the election, which is incredible when you consider that ",["Florida did this mid-decade gerrymander","https://ballotpedia.org/Redistricting_in_Florida_ahead_of_the_2026_elections"]," to try to get them out of a bunch of those seats."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some rural areas of the country were also more competitive than expected, like North Carolina’s 11th Congressional District, where ",["Democrat Jaime Ager flipped a conservative district","https://ncnewsline.com/2026/11/03/democrat-jamie-ager-flips-western-north-carolina-us-house-seat/"],". What does that tell you?"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s definitely an indicator of at least one of these two things. One is just really ",["massive Democratic turnout","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/02/us/politics/early-vote-turnout-senate-battlegrounds.html"]," across the board. Regardless of where they live, Democrats were so enthusiastic and energized to turn out that they did so across all different types of districts and counties."]},{"k":"p","s":["It could also be an indicator of some cross-party voting, where Republicans are crossing over in some cases and voting for the Democrat. I don’t imagine there’s a ton of that, but in a lot of these close districts, and if you’ve got enough of those folks in places like Texas, it really does make a big difference, those small shifts."]},{"k":"p","s":["I think we’re probably also likely to see, and we saw some of this in the exit polling, a major shift in independent voters, unaffiliated voters, toward the Democrats, whereas in 2024 they had been closer to Trump."]},{"k":"p","s":["I’d like to go back to turnout briefly. Turnout looks like it was strong across the country. In Georgia, for example, Election Day’s turnout was on pace to beat turnout in the 2024 presidential elections."]},{"k":"p","s":["That’s unprecedented, at least in modern elections. In Texas, for example, in some counties we saw James Talarico getting as many raw votes as Kamala Harris did in a presidential election. This isn’t a very political science term, but that’s insane. In a midterm election you typically see ",["10% or 15% less turnout","https://usafacts.org/articles/who-shows-up-to-the-midterms/"]," than you would in a presidential election. But Democrats voted in presidential-level numbers in a lot of these really key areas, and that’s explaining how they’re able to overperform at levels we haven’t seen in at least 20 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Elon Musk spent nearly half a billion dollars supporting Republican candidates, including some US$200 million in Texas to elect Ken Paxton for the Senate, who lost. What does that tell you about the influence of political spending?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Republican PACs, super PACs and billionaire donors like Elon Musk may have raised more money compared to Democrats, but ",["Democratic candidates themselves outraised Republican candidates","https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2026/10/16/democratic-candidates-outraise-republicans-gop-megadonors-rush-fill-gap/"]," through donors that gave directly to their campaigns."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is important for a couple of reasons. Number one, because candidates get much better rates on TV ad buys than outside spenders. And so they get more bang for their buck when they’re spending on advertisements, which is the most expensive component of any campaign. And more to the point, that is an indicator of sort of dedicated grassroots donors who turn into voters, whereas Musk gets one vote at the end of the day."]},{"k":"p","s":["And there is no amount of money that can make up for ",["a really flawed candidate like Ken Paxton","https://www.houstonchronicle.com/opinion/editorials/article/yet-more-paxton-scandals-22480142.php"],". And more to the point, a lot of this money, once you get into the tens, the hundreds of millions of dollars, a lot of the research talks about the diminishing returns that you get on that. Going from zero dollars spent to $10 million spent, that’s a very different kind of campaign. But once you go from $500 million to $510 million, that’s not going to get you a whole lot more votes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Any final thoughts?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The territory that Democrats covered is unbelievable. The ",["South Carolina Senate race went to Annie Andrews","https://www.cbsnews.com/news/south-carolina-2026-senate-annie-andrews-darline-graham/"],", the Democrat, which was unfathomable even a few months ago. Mississippi still appears to be somewhat in play. The blue wave turned into something approaching a tsunami. I think a lot of Democrats saw the polling and didn’t want to believe it or couldn’t bring themselves to believe it. But some of this late polling seems to have gotten things on the mark."]},{"k":"p","s":["What we’ve seen in these midterm elections is a massive rebuke of the last two years of the Trump administration, and a sort of blue wave of epic proportions toward the Democrats, the likes of which we haven’t seen in 20 or more years. It’s a huge confirmation of the approach that Democrats took in this election."]}],"chars":5979},"https://theconversation.com/a-global-push-to-become-nature-positive-is-growing-but-can-we-measure-its-progress-297134":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-23T00:37Z","sha":"c51d6f727c0523b6c86514b04ca78151d434303cb4db4f23bb77d1b9276e3d55","read":"https://theconversation.com/a-global-push-to-become-nature-positive-is-growing-but-can-we-measure-its-progress-297134","bytes":183440,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"A global push to become ‘nature positive’ is growing. But can we measure its progress?","by":[{"n":"Maria Armoudian","r":"Associate Professor, Politics & International Relations; Director, Sustainability Hub, University of Auckland, Waipapa Taumata Rau"},{"n":"Carolyn Hogg","r":"Professor of Biodiversity & Conservation and Co-Lead, Australasian Wildlife Genomics Group, University of Sydney"},{"n":"Jill Robbie","r":"Professor of Property Law and the Natural Environment, University of Glasgow"}],"pub":"2026-11-22T23:09:55Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["We rely on nature for everything from food and clean water to medicines, housing and human health. Yet the natural world ",["is in decline","https://www.worldwildlife.org/our-work/wildlife/wwfs-living-planet-report/"],", threatening the ecosystems on which we depend."]},{"k":"p","s":["The economic consequences could be enormous. The World Bank ",["estimates","https://www.worldbank.org/en/topic/environment/publication/the-economic-case-for-nature"]," the partial collapse of key ecosystem services, including pollination and fisheries, could reduce global GDP by US$2.7 trillion annually by 2030."]},{"k":"p","s":["The biodiversity crisis has also featured at this month’s ",["COP31 climate summit","https://unfccc.int/cop31"],", where protecting and restoring ecosystems has been discussed as part of the response to climate change."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2022, governments adopted the ",["Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework","https://www.cbd.int/gbf"],", committing to halt and reverse nature loss by 2030, with a longer-term goal of living in harmony with nature by 2050."]},{"k":"p","s":["The idea of becoming “ ",["nature positive","https://www.naturepositive.org/what-is-nature-positive/"],"” has since gained traction, much as “net zero” has in efforts to tackle climate change."]},{"k":"p","s":["But, as we argue in a new commentary published in the scientific journal ",["Nature","https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03714-8"],", the world needs reliable ways to measure progress towards this goal."]},{"k":"p","s":["If governments, businesses and investors claim their activities are nature positive, how can we tell whether nature is actually recovering?"]},{"k":"h","s":["A common language for nature"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["Nature Positive Initiative","https://www.naturepositive.org/"]," – a global coalition of conservation organisations, businesses and other groups working to halt and reverse nature loss – ",["has proposed","https://www.naturepositive.org/metrics/"]," a set of “state of nature” metrics to track changes in ecosystems and species."]},{"k":"p","s":["The framework considers ecosystem extent, condition and connectivity, as well as species’ extinction risk and population trends. It can be applied at both site and landscape or seascape scales."]},{"k":"p","s":["This marks an important step. The metrics shift attention away from simply reporting actions, such as money spent or trees planted, towards measuring outcomes for nature. A tiered approach allows organisations to begin with basic assessments and progress towards more detailed measurement."]},{"k":"p","s":["The metrics are intended to connect with reporting systems such as the ",["Taskforce on Nature-related Financial Disclosures","https://tnfd.global/knowledge-bank/tnfd-taskforce-on-nature-related-financial-disclosures/"],", an international framework helping businesses assess and report their impacts on nature and the financial risks they face."]},{"k":"p","s":["Embedding nature in corporate risk, investment and disclosure systems could make it harder for decision-makers to ignore environmental damage. Still, disclosure doesn’t guarantee improvement."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Climate-risk reporting","https://theconversation.com/topics/climate-risk-reporting-93384"]," has increased awareness, yet ",["evidence","https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10551-022-05292-x"]," that disclosure alone reduces emissions remains limited. Nature reporting could encounter the same problem: organisations may become better at describing damage without changing the activities causing it."]},{"k":"h","s":["Nature doesn’t fit neatly into a spreadsheet"]},{"k":"p","s":["The proposed metrics are better understood as a broad framework than as a finished set of standardised measurements. Organisations still have freedom to decide what to measure and how."]},{"k":"p","s":["That flexibility creates risks. A company could select ecosystems or species that are easy to monitor, while overlooking other losses. An increase in vegetation cover might look positive on paper but say little about ecological function, habitat quality or whether culturally important species are recovering."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nature is dynamic. Ecosystems change over time. Recovery is rarely linear, and endless improvement is neither realistic nor always desirable. In a healthy or mature ecosystem, maintaining its condition may be a better outcome than showing continual gains."]},{"k":"p","s":["Global consistency also has limits. Nature loss is a global problem, but it occurs in local places. Global datasets ",["can miss local ecological change","https://earth.org/research-gap-the-geographical-bias-of-environmental-data/"],", especially in data-poor regions. They can also override local knowledge and priorities if used without on-ground assessment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Importantly, nature-positive claims cannot be credible if Indigenous rights, cultural authority and ",["data sovereignty","https://www.gida-global.org/careprinciples"]," are bypassed. Metrics influence where money flows, which species and landscapes receive attention, and who bears the costs. They are not socially or politically neutral."]},{"k":"h","s":["Testing the system while putting it to work"]},{"k":"p","s":["These shortcomings are not reasons to abandon the state-of-nature framework. Waiting for a perfect system while nature continues to decline would be damaging."]},{"k":"p","s":["The framework needs to be put into practice and independently evaluated at the same time. Its credibility will depend on what it delivers in the real world."]},{"k":"p","s":["The metrics should now be tested across protected areas, farms, restoration sites, community-managed landscapes and places affected by mining, forestry and other industries. Testing must span different ecosystems, legal, financial and governance arrangements."]},{"k":"p","s":["Researchers should work with Indigenous peoples, local communities, land managers, governments, businesses and investors to co-develop monitoring approaches."]},{"k":"p","s":["Combining field data, long-term monitoring and local ecological knowledge can all help reveal where the framework works, where it fails and what needs to change."]},{"k":"p","s":["Academic, government and industry partnerships could help provide this independent scrutiny, while turning research findings into practical guidance for those using the framework. Such evaluations also need to consider the wider consequences of nature-positive projects."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nature positive could become a powerful force for change. But success should be judged by recovering ecosystems and thriving communities – not by the number of reports produced."]},{"k":"p","s":["The task now is to test, improve and use the metrics in the real world, before nature loses what no framework can restore."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authors acknowledge the contributions of Chris Elphick, Jacqueline Beggs, Catherine Price, Eleanor Bruce, Bruce Burns, John Finch, Rodrigo Arriagada, Maria Santos, Britta Sjöstedt, Nicholas Ngepah and Rob Ogden; and other colleagues participating in this work from the University of Sydney, University of Glasgow, University of Auckland, University of Zurich, Lund University, University of Johannesburg, Universitas Gadjah Mada, UC Chile, University of Connecticut, Korea University and the University of Edinburgh."]}],"chars":6021},"https://theconversation.com/energy-and-climate-have-been-overlooked-at-victorias-election-but-theres-a-lot-at-stake-295871":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-24T22:39Z","sha":"9fad41d3167426a8f41b0d8538622bf1b67b02e9afabd251a5603577e36c75ca","read":"https://theconversation.com/energy-and-climate-have-been-overlooked-at-victorias-election-but-theres-a-lot-at-stake-295871","bytes":186004,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Energy and climate have been overlooked at Victoria’s election – but there’s a lot at stake","by":[{"n":"David Karoly","r":"Professor Emeritus in Climate Science, The University of Melbourne"},{"n":"Andrew B. Watkins","r":"Adjunct Professor (Practice) in Climate Science, School of Earth, Atmosphere and Environment, Monash University"}],"pub":"2026-11-24T21:37:30Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["State elections don’t often get this much attention. But the votes cast by Victorians for November 28th’s election will have greater resonance this year."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Potholes","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-24/victorian-election-parties-pothole-promises/107416310"],", ",["costly infrastructure projects","https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/08/big-build-royal-commission-victorian-election-ben-carroll-labor-ntwnfb"]," and the ",["cost of living","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-18/cost-of-living-voting-vic-state-election-food-relief/107382428"]," are dominating election coverage so far."]},{"k":"p","s":["Amid these issues, it’s easy to overlook crucial climate and energy policies. If the longstanding Labor government is swept from power in Victoria, the new government is likely to roll back climate action measures."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Coalition has taken a stance against net zero and key transmission line projects, while One Nation is ",["strongly opposed","https://onenation.org.au/policies/net-zero-is-destroying-australia"]," to renewables, net zero and the Paris Agreement."]},{"k":"h","s":["What progress has Victoria made?"]},{"k":"p","s":["When Labor took office in Victoria in 2014, renewables provided about 11% of Victoria’s power. Now, 12 years later, that figure is more than 44%. Labor ",["recently approved","https://reneweconomy.com.au/state-approves-six-new-wind-and-battery-projects-before-going-into-election-caretaker-mode/"]," large new ",["wind farms","https://www.premier.vic.gov.au/labor-approves-southern-hemispheres-biggest-wind-farm"]," and battery projects."]},{"k":"p","s":["While positive, there are ",["real question marks","https://theenergy.co/articles/victorian-energy-security-hangs-in-the-balance"]," over the future. Ageing coal plants are soon ",["to retire","https://reneweconomy.com.au/too-old-cant-dance-new-numbers-show-yallourn-is-ready-to-retire/"],". Victoria has long been the most gas-reliant state, but the wells in Bass Strait are almost empty."]},{"k":"p","s":["Labor’s plan to reduce the state’s reliance on fossil gas is showing ",["some success","https://reneweconomy.com.au/household-gas-use-is-falling-much-faster-than-connections-new-data-shows-as-quiet-quitting-takes-hold/"],", but the pace of transition is slow."]},{"k":"h","s":["What are major parties promising?"]},{"k":"p","s":["At this election, Labor has largely downplayed energy and climate policies. The government has announced ",["two new","https://www.premier.vic.gov.au/securing-more-gas-back-jobs-and-bring-down-costs"]," ",["gas projects","https://www.premier.vic.gov.au/backing-victorian-gas-keep-prices-low"],", claiming they will bring down costs for consumers."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Coalition is similarly focused on finding ",["new supplies of gas","https://www.vicliberal.org.au/media-releases/2026-08-19-more-gas-fewer-poles-and-wires-our-plan-to-keep-the-lights-on-and-prices-low"],". It also wants to keep coal plants “ ",["running as long and hard as possible","https://www.liberal.org.au/our-plan/energy"],"”."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Coalition has promised to ",["scrap","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-08-19/victorian-coalition-promises-to-scrap-vni-west-transmission-line/107053638"]," a major new transmission line meant to boost renewables and strengthen the grid."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Coalition isn’t totally opposed to renewables – it has ",["flagged plans","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-05-07/victoria-election-coalition-vows-to-pause-transmission-projects/106651434"]," for new urban solar parks and to support business to go solar."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Greens ",["are promising","https://greens.org.au/vic/policies/energy-policy"]," a faster transition to renewables, sharper emissions cuts and the removal of fossil fuel subsidies."]},{"k":"p","s":["One Nation ",["has pledged","https://vic.onenation.org.au/policies/energy"]," to scrap all net-zero targets and subsidies, cancel two major transmission line projects, seek more local gas and push to remove the ban on nuclear power."]},{"k":"p","s":["In June, One Nation leader Pauline Hanson even ",["declared","https://thenightly.com.au/politics/pauline-hansons-full-speech-at-the-national-press-club--c-22444111"]," “global warming is a hoax” – a line borrowed from US President ",["Donald Trump","https://news.un.org/en/story/2025/09/1165924"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["An important reminder of the science"]},{"k":"p","s":["What can get lost in political debates is how the science of the greenhouse effect is ",["extremely well established","https://history.aip.org/climate/timeline.htm"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s more than 200 years since French mathematician Joseph Fourier realised Earth’s distance from the sun should have led to a much colder planet. In 1822, he proposed the greenhouse effect to explain it – the fact that gases in the atmosphere trap heat and warm the planet. By the 1850s, scientists had figured out one gas was particularly important – carbon dioxide."]},{"k":"p","s":["Without greenhouse gases, our planet would be a ball of ice, hovering around -18°C. These potent gases stop a great deal of the sun’s heat from escaping, despite only making up ",["~0.1% of the atmosphere","https://www.noaa.gov/jetstream/atmosphere"],". This is why we have a very liveable global average temperature of +15°C."]},{"k":"p","s":["The problem is, humans have rapidly increased the volume of these potent warming gases, largely by turning long-buried carbon (in the form of coal, oil and gas) into atmospheric CO₂, methane and other greenhouse gases."]},{"k":"p","s":["Over the last 800,000 years, atmospheric CO₂ hovered around 280 parts per million (ppm). After we started burning fossil fuels, it ",["climbed past 300ppm","https://www.climate.gov/news-features/understanding-climate/climate-change-atmospheric-carbon-dioxide"],". CO₂ levels are now at 425 ppm – an increase of more than 50% in just a century."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 1896, Swedish scientist Svante Arrhenius calculated if atmospheric CO₂ doubled, it would warm the earth ",["about 5-6°C","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.endeavour.2016.07.002"],". We now know that figure is very likely to be ",["between 2 and 5°C","https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/faqs/IPCC_AR6_WGI_FAQ_Chapter_07.pdf"],")."]},{"k":"p","s":["Scientific hoaxes rarely last two months, let alone two centuries. As our data gathering methods have improved, ever more proof has come in. Satellites can now directly measure the energy ",["trapped by greenhouse gases","https://doi.org/10.5194/essd-15-1675-2023"],", giving us clear, empirical evidence that the world is getting rapidly hotter."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many other lines of evidence converge showing the ",["fingerprint of climate change","https://maths.anu.edu.au/files/CMAProcVol25-Karoly.pdf"],", from Antarctic ice cores to melting glaciers and sea ice to rising sea levels."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is why the world’s climate scientists ",["can state","https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/chapter/chapter-3/#Synthesis"]," it is “unequivocal that human influence has warmed the atmosphere, ocean and land since pre-industrial times”."]},{"k":"p","s":["We are undeniably trashing our own home by increasing climate pollution. Calling climate change a hoax must be called for what it is – disinformation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Victoria is not immune to climate change"]},{"k":"p","s":["At a federal level, the Labor government acknowledges climate change is an urgent and existential problem. The extent of the threats were made clear last year when Climate Minister Chris Bowen released the ",["National Climate Risk Assessment","https://minister.dcceew.gov.au/bowen/media-releases/cascading-compounding-and-concurrent-national-climate-risk-assessment-shows-why-climate-action-so-important"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the government has taken ",["limited action","https://theconversation.com/its-been-one-year-since-australia-assessed-its-national-climate-risk-but-have-we-listened-291364"]," since, approving ",["several more coal and gas projects","https://www.climatecouncil.org.au/resources/albanese-governments-fossil-fuel-approvals/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["It doesn’t matter where oil, gas or coal is burned. Greenhouses gases enter the same atmosphere we all share. Every government must accept accountability for every tonne of CO₂ extracted from their lands and seas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Victoria faces many climate risks, as the assessment made very clear. If the world warms 3°C by 2100, heat-related deaths in Melbourne will more than double, according to the assessment."]},{"k":"p","s":["By 2050, the state could see almost A$30 billion dollars each year in insured losses due to climate extremes, according to the assessment. That figure includes $18.7 billion due to bushfire, $6.9 billion due to floods and $5.6 billion due to storm damage."]},{"k":"p","s":["Rising seas and storm surges are projected to cost Victorians living on the coast at least ",["$167 billion by 2100","https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-026-67957-1"],". Half of these costs are due to direct impact on coastal properties."]},{"k":"p","s":["In recent months, there’s been a backlash against pro-fossil fuel politics in ",["Brazil","https://atmos.earth/political-landscapes/is-brazils-vote-a-turning-point-for-climate-politics/"]," and the ",["United States","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ce85709xdk4o"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If Victoria bucks the trend and votes to scrap existing clean energy policies, it would be a clear backward step. Any savings from supporting fossil fuels today will be dwarfed by the costs we will pass to future generations."]}],"chars":5969},"https://theconversation.com/the-worlds-ice-is-in-real-peril-from-climate-change-and-will-keep-melting-even-if-we-reach-net-zero-297062":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-27T05:55Z","sha":"fb4e3504e64cc75e3d773a31ff69c74b40755d96a869b1a2e3e8b74191d015a8","read":"https://theconversation.com/the-worlds-ice-is-in-real-peril-from-climate-change-and-will-keep-melting-even-if-we-reach-net-zero-297062","bytes":178449,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"The world’s ice is in real peril from climate change – and will keep melting even if we reach net zero","by":[{"n":"Jon Cox","r":"Proposal Development Manager, Securing Antarctica’s Environmental Future, Monash University"},{"n":"Andrew Mackintosh","r":"Chief Investigator, Antarctic Environmental Science, Monash University"}],"pub":"2026-11-27T04:21:12Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["In 2015, the world agreed to work to hold climate change below 1.5°C. But that goal is no longer possible."]},{"k":"p","s":["Earth will pass 1.5°C ",["by 2030","https://theconversation.com/the-world-will-soon-shoot-past-1-5-c-what-does-this-mean-294577"],". Some years are already over 1.5°C warmer than the pre-industrial average. This means we are set for climate overshoot – heading for even more dangerous levels of climate change."]},{"k":"p","s":["Are there ways of temporarily going past 1.5°C and then pulling carbon dioxide back out of the atmosphere to return us to a safer temperature? In a September ",["report","https://www.unep.org/en/publications/report/limiting-overshoot-navigating-exceedance-15degc-and-pathways-towards-return"],", experts from the United Nations Environment Programme point out this would rely on sustained net-negative emissions, likely to be slow and uncertain."]},{"k":"p","s":["We might assume net-negative emissions would mean planetary systems will start to return to a climatic “safe operating space” of the relatively stable 11,700 years prior to our time, during which human civilisation developed and flourished."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ice sheets regulate the climate in three ways. They reflect solar energy back to space, due to their great height which cools the atmosphere and influences global wind patterns. They also regulate the climate via ocean circulation through their input of cold fresh water, and their control on sea levels."]},{"k":"p","s":["Concerning ",["new research","https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aef5636"]," shows the world’s ice will keep melting, even if we reach net-negative emissions quickly."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ice has a memory"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many parts of the cryosphere have a long memory. So if the melting of glaciers and ice sheets hits critical thresholds, it will lock in centuries of sea-level rise – even if the world’s emissions have become net-negative."]},{"k":"p","s":[["New research","https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aef5636"]," shows the world’s sea ice, snow and permafrost are already outside the previously stable climatic envelope, meaning that losses may be irreversible. The authors find that land ice as a whole (the combination of glaciers and ice sheets) has not yet crossed into unsafe territory. However, because land ice responds slowly, enough losses are now locked in to cause dangerously advancing sea levels by the end of the century."]},{"k":"p","s":["Almost 90% of the world’s land ice is locked up ",["in Antarctica","https://www.antarctica.gov.au/about-antarctica/ice-and-atmosphere/ice-sheet/"],". Scientists published ",["research","https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-026-10614-4"]," this year showing that current rates of Antarctic ice loss strongly predict its contribution to sea level rise over the next three to five decades, after which it may accelerate. The predictability identified in this research does not reduce long-term risk, but merely provides us with a defined period in which to act with greater confidence. Improvements in observational systems and ice sheet model developments will directly translate into more reliable sea level projections for short-term planning horizons."]},{"k":"p","s":["Land ice in other areas are also showing signs of rapid change. Glaciers are retreating at accelerating rates across nearly every part of the planet. In the European Alps, ",["Switzerland’s glaciers","https://doi.glamos.ch/pubs/annualrep/annualrep_2026.html"]," lost 5.5% of their ice this year alone. Since 2021, almost 20% of these glaciers have melted. Melt rates between 2022-26 are more than double any five-year period previously monitored. Globally, glaciers are predicted to lose ",["about 40%","https://doi.org/10.1126/science.adu4675"]," of their current mass even if global temperatures stablise at current conditions, and considerably more under future warming scenarios."]},{"k":"p","s":["In August, over 130 million cubic metres of ",["rock and ice","https://theconversation.com/tsunami-of-dirt-what-caused-nepals-deadly-glacial-flood-290615"]," broke away from the Himalayan mountain Langtang Lirung in Nepal. The resulting ice avalanche triggered devastating flooding, leaving thousands of people dead or missing. Ice melt likely contributed, as melting permafrost makes mountain slopes less stable, while glacier retreat can also destabilise slopes. Such huge ",["cascading disasters","https://theconversation.com/nepals-flash-floods-show-the-devastating-power-of-cascading-hazards-290611"]," involve multiple triggers, including the mobilisation of rock, ice, sediment and water, making risk management more complex."]},{"k":"p","s":["The cryosphere is in increasing trouble, with ",["substantial declines","https://www.science.org/content/article/both-poles-warm-water-eating-away-sea-ice-below"]," and record lows in both Arctic and Antarctic sea ice in the last decade. But it is still possible that very rapid emissions cuts will allow the cryosphere to remain within the envelope of a safe operating space, with sea level rise impacts reduced, or spread out across centuries or even millennia. That’s according to a new United Nations ",["report","https://iccinet.org/overshoot/"],", released this month."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Tsunami of dirt: what caused Nepal’s deadly glacial flood?","https://theconversation.com/tsunami-of-dirt-what-caused-nepals-deadly-glacial-flood-290615"]]},{"k":"h","s":["The crucial cryosphere"]},{"k":"p","s":["For years, scientists have tracked dangerous levels of change using the ",["planetary boundaries framework","https://doi.org/10.1126/sciadv.adh2458"],". It lays out nine boundaries showing the danger levels for processes crucial to keeping Earth systems stable, such as climate change and biodiversity."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite its importance in regulating temperatures and the water cycle, among other things, the cryosphere isn’t tracked as a whole. Its functions have been partly absorbed into climate, freshwater and land system boundaries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Researchers are ",["calling for","https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aef5636"]," the health of the cryosphere as a whole to be tracked and reported on."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s abundantly clear the cryosphere is in real decline. As the world prepares to breach 1.5°C, cutting emissions sharply is crucial."]},{"k":"p","s":["What researchers have shown this year, however, is that ice has a long memory. We may be able to return some parts of the cryosphere to a safer space, but others will be harder. Climate adaptation will be key to prepare societies for the long-term effects of melting ice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Ice shelves hold back Antarctica’s glaciers from adding to sea levels – but they’re crumbling","https://theconversation.com/ice-shelves-hold-back-antarcticas-glaciers-from-adding-to-sea-levels-but-theyre-crumbling-185509"]]}],"chars":5257}};
